*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* DAC0800 / DAC0802 - 8-bit multiplying current-output D/A converter
* Behavioral ("functional") macromodel for LTspice.
*
* Based on:
*   Texas Instruments (National Semiconductor), "DAC0800/DAC0802 8-Bit
*   Digital-to-Analog Converters", SNAS538C - June 1999, revised Feb 2013
*
* This is NOT a transistor-level model.  Every block of the Block Diagram
* (Figure 4) is reproduced by its terminal behaviour - reference amplifier,
* reference current source, eight current switches, complementary outputs -
* with the numbers taken from the Electrical Characteristics table (TYPICAL
* column) and from the typical curves.  The point is to simulate the DAC as
* part of a circuit: op-amp output stages, bipolar offsets, multiplying
* references, a SAR or a waveform generator.
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* PIN ORDER  (16-lead PDIP pin order; the SOIC package numbers the same
* signals differently - the port ORDER below is what matters)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*   1  VLC    threshold control (logic threshold = VLC + 1.4 V)
*   2  IOUTB  complementary current output (IOUT bar)
*   3  VM     negative supply V-
*   4  IOUT   current output
*   5  B1     MSB          9  B5
*   6  B2                 10  B6
*   7  B3                 11  B7
*   8  B4                 12  B8   LSB
*  13  VP     positive supply V+
*  14  VREFP  reference input + (the reference current flows INTO this pin)
*  15  VREFN  reference input -
*  16  COMP   reference amplifier compensation (capacitor to V-)
*
*   X1 VLC IOUTB VM IOUT B1 B2 B3 B4 B5 B6 B7 B8 VP VREFP VREFN COMP DAC0800
*
*   IFS = (VREF/RREF)*255/256,  IOUT = IREF*code/256,
*   IOUT + IOUTB = IFS for every code (Figure 18)
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* WHAT IS MODELLED
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  * Reference amplifier (pins 14, 15, 16): a transconductance stage drives
*    the COMP node, which sets the reference current IREF sunk at pin 14,
*    so the loop forces V(14) = V(15).  Its DC gain makes the error ~0.1 mV.
*    The loop is a single pole set by the internal 5 pF plus your CC:
*    ~3 MHz with CC = 15 pF and 1 k at pin 14 (Figure 7), very slow and
*    quiet with the recommended CC = 0.01 uF (Figure 18).  Large-signal
*    slew 8 mA/us with no CC (dI/dt typ, Figure 26).  Reference bias
*    current 1 uA out of pin 15 (I15).
*  * Reference current range: 4.2 mA max for V- = -8 .. -18 V, 2.1 mA for
*    V- = -5 V (IFSR, Figure 5), soft limit.  Reference common-mode range
*    down to V- + 4.5 V (Figure 8 at 2 mA): below it IREF collapses.
*  * Current switches: B1 (MSB) .. B8 (LSB) weigh IREF/2 .. IREF/256; a bit
*    that is on goes to IOUT, off to IOUTB; the remaining 1/256 is the R-2R
*    termination, so IOUT + IOUTB = IFS = IREF*255/256.  The weights are
*    ideal (nonlinearity and full-scale error are inside the typical +-1/2
*    LSB of the datasheet).  Zero-scale current 0.2 uA (IZS) on each output.
*  * Logic inputs: threshold VLC + 1.4 V (Figure 10, 25 C), each bit fully
*    switched within +-0.1 V of it (Figure 13).  2 uA flows OUT of an input
*    held low, ~0 when high (IIL, IIH, Figure 9).
*  * Switching: each bit ramps between its two outputs in 70 ns, so the
*    output crosses 50 % 35 ns after the input (tPLH / tPHL typ) and is
*    within 1/2 LSB in ~90 ns (ts typ 100 ns), for any code change.
*  * Output compliance: each output sinks its current down to V- + 4.5 V
*    (-10.5 V with V- = -15 V: the -10 V of the table, Figure 11 at 2 mA)
*    and up to any positive voltage (+18 V in the table).  The 1 - 2 V of
*    extra range a lower IREF gives (Figures 8, 11) is not modelled.
*  * Supply currents: I+ = 2.2 mA + 10 uA/V*(V+ - V-) (2.3 / 2.4 / 2.5 mA at
*    10 / 20 / 30 V, the table), and I- = I+ + IREF + IOUT + IOUTB - the
*    reference and output currents return through V-, so I- = I+ + 2*IREF
*    (4.3 / 6.4 / 6.5 mA, the table).
*  * The reference current limit and its common-mode range are referred to
*    the height of pin 15 above V- (pin 15 is normally at ground, and the
*    loop holds pin 14 at the same voltage).
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* WHAT IS NOT MODELLED  (behavioural model - know the limits)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  * No temperature model (TCIFS, threshold drift of Figure 10).
*  * Ideal bit weights: no nonlinearity, no full-scale error, no full-scale
*    symmetry error, no glitch at major carries (all bits move together).
*  * Output resistance (> 20 Mohm) and output capacitance are not in the
*    datasheet: 1 Gohm leakage and COUT = 5 pF (assumed) on each output.
*  * The positive common-mode limit of the reference amplifier (V+ - 1.5 V),
*    the logic-input range (-10 .. +18 V), the 36 V / 5 mA / 4.25 mA
*    absolute maximum ratings and the power supply sensitivity are not
*    policed.  The reference current cannot go negative (as in the part).
*  * The SOIC package pin numbering (same subcircuit, other pin numbers).
*  * A floating logic input reads HIGH here (its 2 uA charges it up).
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* PARAMETERS  (override per instance:  X1 ... DAC0800 TSW=100 IZS=1u)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  VTHO     logic threshold above VLC, V                     (1.4)
*  VTHW     half-width of the bit transition, V              (0.1)
*  TSW      bit switching ramp, ns (tpd = TSW/2)             (70)
*  IIL      current out of a low logic input                 (2 uA)
*  CIN      logic input capacitance (assumed)                (2 pF)
*  IZS      zero-scale current on each output                (0.2 uA)
*  COUT     output capacitance (assumed)                     (5 pF)
*  GM1      reference amplifier transconductance             (0.4 mS)
*  I1MAX    its output current limit (sets the 8 mA/us slew) (40 uA)
*  CINT     internal compensation capacitance                (5 pF)
*  GM2      reference current per volt on COMP               (1 mA/V)
*  VCMN     compliance and reference CM limit above V-      (4.5 V)
*  IBREF    reference bias current out of pin 15             (1 uA)
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------

.SUBCKT DAC0800 VLC IOUTB VM IOUT B1 B2 B3 B4 B5 B6 B7 B8 VP VREFP VREFN COMP
+ VTHO=1.4 VTHW=0.1 TSW=70 IIL=2u CIN=2p IZS=0.2u COUT=5p
+ GM1=0.4m I1MAX=40u CINT=5p GM2=1m VCMN=4.5 IBREF=1u

*==============================================================================
* SUPPLY
*   bias current V+ -> V- (table: 2.3 / 2.4 / 2.5 mA at 10 / 20 / 30 V)
*==============================================================================
Bsup  VP VM I = (2.2m + 10u*V(VP,VM))*min(1, uramp(V(VP,VM))/5)

*==============================================================================
* REFERENCE AMPLIFIER AND REFERENCE CURRENT
*   gm stage: I = I1MAX*tanh(GM1*(V14-V15)/I1MAX) into COMP (CINT + your CC
*   to V-, 100 Mohm for a finite DC gain), soft-clamped to V- .. V- + 8 V.
*   Reference current sunk at pin 14:
*     Ilin = GM2*(V(COMP)-V- - 1.4 V)          (>= 0)
*     IREF = Ilin / (1 + (Ilin/Imax)^8)^(1/8)  (soft limit at Imax(V-))
*     Imax = 2.1 mA at V- = -5 V .. 4.2 mA at V- <= -8 V (Figure 5)
*   and it collapses when pin 15 gets within VCMN of V-.
*==============================================================================
* (+ 0.1 % of GM1 linear: a saturated stage still has a slope, so Newton
*  finds the operating point; it adds 0.4 uA/V of overdrive to the slew)
Bea   VM COMP I = {I1MAX}*tanh({GM1}*V(VREFP,VREFN)/{I1MAX}) + 1m*{GM1}*V(VREFP,VREFN)
Cint  COMP VM {CINT}
Rint  COMP VM 100Meg
Bccl  COMP VM I = 1m*(uramp(V(COMP,VM)-8) - uramp(-V(COMP,VM)))
* reference bias current out of pin 15
Bib   VP VREFN I = {IBREF}*min(1, uramp(V(VP,VM))/5)

* control: Ilin = GM2*(V(COMP)-V- - 1.4 V), >= 0 (+0.1 % linear below, so
* that it is never flat while Newton looks for the operating point)
Bilin n_ilin VM V = 1e3*{GM2}*(uramp(V(COMP,VM)-1.4) + 1m*(V(COMP,VM)-1.4))
* Imax in mA (node volts): 2.1 mA at |V-| = 5 V, 4.2 mA at |V-| >= 8 V,
* |V-| taken as the height of pin 15 above V- (pin 15 is normally at
* ground, and the loop holds pin 14 at the same voltage)
Bvmag n_vmag VM V = uramp(V(VREFN,VM))
Bimax n_imax VM V = min(4.2, max(0.2, 2.1*min(1,V(n_vmag,VM)/5) + 0.7*uramp(V(n_vmag,VM)-5)))
* IREF in mA (node volts), soft-limited at Imax (+0.1 % slope beyond)
Biref n_iref VM V = V(n_ilin,VM)/pow(1 + pow(V(n_ilin,VM)/V(n_imax,VM),8), 0.125) + 1m*V(n_ilin,VM)
* reference headroom (Figure 8): IREF collapses with pin 15 below V- + VCMN
Bkr   n_kr VM V = min(1, max(0, (V(VREFN,VM) - {VCMN})/0.3))
Bref  VREFP VM I = 1m*V(n_iref,VM)*V(n_kr,VM)
Cref  VREFP VM 2p
Rref  VREFP VM 1G

*==============================================================================
* LOGIC INPUTS  (threshold VLC + VTHO, linear over +-VTHW)
*   a low input sources IIL (out of the pin), a high one ~0 (Figure 9)
*   each digitised bit d_k ramps (b_k) between 0 and 1 in TSW ns:
*   a slew-limited follower written as  b = d - y,  C dy/dt = C dd/dt -
*   G*slope(y)  - at DC y = 0 exactly, the operating point needs no search.
*==============================================================================
Bd1  n_d1 VM V = min(1, max(0, (V(B1,VLC)-{VTHO})/(2*{VTHW}) + 0.5))
Bd2  n_d2 VM V = min(1, max(0, (V(B2,VLC)-{VTHO})/(2*{VTHW}) + 0.5))
Bd3  n_d3 VM V = min(1, max(0, (V(B3,VLC)-{VTHO})/(2*{VTHW}) + 0.5))
Bd4  n_d4 VM V = min(1, max(0, (V(B4,VLC)-{VTHO})/(2*{VTHW}) + 0.5))
Bd5  n_d5 VM V = min(1, max(0, (V(B5,VLC)-{VTHO})/(2*{VTHW}) + 0.5))
Bd6  n_d6 VM V = min(1, max(0, (V(B6,VLC)-{VTHO})/(2*{VTHW}) + 0.5))
Bd7  n_d7 VM V = min(1, max(0, (V(B7,VLC)-{VTHO})/(2*{VTHW}) + 0.5))
Bd8  n_d8 VM V = min(1, max(0, (V(B8,VLC)-{VTHO})/(2*{VTHW}) + 0.5))
* input current: IIL out of a low input (needs a live V+)
Bi1  VP B1 I = {IIL}*(1-V(n_d1,VM))*min(1, uramp(V(VP,B1))/0.5)
Bi2  VP B2 I = {IIL}*(1-V(n_d2,VM))*min(1, uramp(V(VP,B2))/0.5)
Bi3  VP B3 I = {IIL}*(1-V(n_d3,VM))*min(1, uramp(V(VP,B3))/0.5)
Bi4  VP B4 I = {IIL}*(1-V(n_d4,VM))*min(1, uramp(V(VP,B4))/0.5)
Bi5  VP B5 I = {IIL}*(1-V(n_d5,VM))*min(1, uramp(V(VP,B5))/0.5)
Bi6  VP B6 I = {IIL}*(1-V(n_d6,VM))*min(1, uramp(V(VP,B6))/0.5)
Bi7  VP B7 I = {IIL}*(1-V(n_d7,VM))*min(1, uramp(V(VP,B7))/0.5)
Bi8  VP B8 I = {IIL}*(1-V(n_d8,VM))*min(1, uramp(V(VP,B8))/0.5)
Ci1  B1 VLC {CIN}
Ci2  B2 VLC {CIN}
Ci3  B3 VLC {CIN}
Ci4  B4 VLC {CIN}
Ci5  B5 VLC {CIN}
Ci6  B6 VLC {CIN}
Ci7  B7 VLC {CIN}
Ci8  B8 VLC {CIN}
Ri1  B1 VM 10G
Ri2  B2 VM 10G
Ri3  B3 VM 10G
Ri4  B4 VM 10G
Ri5  B5 VM 10G
Ri6  B6 VM 10G
Ri7  B7 VM 10G
Ri8  B8 VM 10G
* switching ramps: slope 1/TSW [1/ns], linear inside 0.1 of error
Cy1  n_d1 n_y1 1p
By1  n_y1 VM I = 1m/{TSW}*(min(1,10*uramp(V(n_y1,VM))) - min(1,10*uramp(-V(n_y1,VM))))
Ry1  n_y1 VM 1G
Cy2  n_d2 n_y2 1p
By2  n_y2 VM I = 1m/{TSW}*(min(1,10*uramp(V(n_y2,VM))) - min(1,10*uramp(-V(n_y2,VM))))
Ry2  n_y2 VM 1G
Cy3  n_d3 n_y3 1p
By3  n_y3 VM I = 1m/{TSW}*(min(1,10*uramp(V(n_y3,VM))) - min(1,10*uramp(-V(n_y3,VM))))
Ry3  n_y3 VM 1G
Cy4  n_d4 n_y4 1p
By4  n_y4 VM I = 1m/{TSW}*(min(1,10*uramp(V(n_y4,VM))) - min(1,10*uramp(-V(n_y4,VM))))
Ry4  n_y4 VM 1G
Cy5  n_d5 n_y5 1p
By5  n_y5 VM I = 1m/{TSW}*(min(1,10*uramp(V(n_y5,VM))) - min(1,10*uramp(-V(n_y5,VM))))
Ry5  n_y5 VM 1G
Cy6  n_d6 n_y6 1p
By6  n_y6 VM I = 1m/{TSW}*(min(1,10*uramp(V(n_y6,VM))) - min(1,10*uramp(-V(n_y6,VM))))
Ry6  n_y6 VM 1G
Cy7  n_d7 n_y7 1p
By7  n_y7 VM I = 1m/{TSW}*(min(1,10*uramp(V(n_y7,VM))) - min(1,10*uramp(-V(n_y7,VM))))
Ry7  n_y7 VM 1G
Cy8  n_d8 n_y8 1p
By8  n_y8 VM I = 1m/{TSW}*(min(1,10*uramp(V(n_y8,VM))) - min(1,10*uramp(-V(n_y8,VM))))
Ry8  n_y8 VM 1G
* fraction of IREF steered to IOUT:  sum b_k / 2^k
Bcode n_code VM V = (V(n_d1,VM)-V(n_y1,VM))/2 + (V(n_d2,VM)-V(n_y2,VM))/4
+   + (V(n_d3,VM)-V(n_y3,VM))/8 + (V(n_d4,VM)-V(n_y4,VM))/16
+   + (V(n_d5,VM)-V(n_y5,VM))/32 + (V(n_d6,VM)-V(n_y6,VM))/64
+   + (V(n_d7,VM)-V(n_y7,VM))/128 + (V(n_d8,VM)-V(n_y8,VM))/256

*==============================================================================
* CURRENT OUTPUTS  (both sink current into the part, returned through V-)
*   IOUT  = IREF*code/256 + IZS,   IOUTB = IREF*(255-code)/256 + IZS
*   each one only while its pin is above V- + VCMN (0.3 V soft)
*==============================================================================
Bko   n_ko VM V = min(1, max(0, (V(IOUT,VM)  - {VCMN})/0.3))
Bkob  n_kob VM V = min(1, max(0, (V(IOUTB,VM) - {VCMN})/0.3))
Bout  IOUT  VM I = (1m*V(n_iref,VM)*V(n_kr,VM)*V(n_code,VM) + {IZS})*V(n_ko,VM)
Boutb IOUTB VM I = (1m*V(n_iref,VM)*V(n_kr,VM)*(255/256 - V(n_code,VM)) + {IZS})*V(n_kob,VM)
* pulled further down than that, the saturated switch conducts back out of
* the pin (1 mS) - it also gives Newton a slope there
Bclo  VM IOUT  I = 1m*uramp({VCMN} - 2 - V(IOUT,VM))
Bclob VM IOUTB I = 1m*uramp({VCMN} - 2 - V(IOUTB,VM))
Co    IOUT  VM {COUT}
Cob   IOUTB VM {COUT}
Ro    IOUT  VM 1G
Rob   IOUTB VM 1G
* threshold-control pin: no current specified; 1 Gohm keeps it defined
Rvlc  VLC VM 1G

.ENDS DAC0800
